{"hw":"φροντιστής","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">φροντιστής</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">φροντ-ιστής</span>, <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">οῦ</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">ὁ</span>, <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">deep thinker,</b> as Socrates is called in derision by <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Nu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">266</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">414</span> </span> (anap.), al.; <span class=\"gk\">φ. τῶν μετεώρων, τῶν οὐρανίων,</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">one who meditates on</b> supra-terrestrial things, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Smp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">6.6</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Mem.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.7.6</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τὰ.. μετέωρα φ.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ap.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">18b</span> </span>: hence, generally, <b class=\"lex-tr\">philosopher,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Smp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.2</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hsch.</span> </span> </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">one who takes care of,</b> <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">τινων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.S.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">37.8</span> </span>; <b class=\"lex-tr\">curator,</b> <span class=\"gk\">ἱεροῦ Ἀφροδίτης</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IGRom.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.1167<em>C</em>4</span> </span> (Egypt, <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">ii A. D.</span>); <span class=\"gk\">συναγωγῆς</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">JHS</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">28.195</span> </span> (Side), cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">BMus.Inscr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1069</span> </span> (Fayum, <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">ii A.D.</span>); <span class=\"gk\">τῶν δημοσίων πραγμάτων</span> Sch.<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pl.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">908</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τῶν ἀρχομένων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Poll.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.40</span> </span>: <b class=\"lex-tr\">manager,</b> <span class=\"gk\">κακῷ φ. τὰ καθ' ἑαυτοὺς ἐπιτρέψομεν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Porph.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Abst.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.50</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">παρύγρων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Cat.Cod.Astr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">8(1).177</span> </span>; without gen., <b class=\"lex-tr\">manager, housekeeper,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Phld.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Oec.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">p.51</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">J.</span> </span>: as transl. of Lat. <b class=\"lex-tr\">procurator,</b> <span class=\"gk\">ὁ φ. Δρούσου</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IGRom.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.219</span> </span> (Ilium). </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">2</span> title of official of a <span class=\"gk\">φρατρία,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">14.759.8</span> </span> (Naples). </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">3</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">bailiff, house-steward,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Gp.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.8.1</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">BGU</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">603.2</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">(ii A. D.)</span>, etc.</div></div>"}